{"title":"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sandy’s Fruit Market sells cherries, plums and blueberries. For each type of fruit, the price of one box is shown in the table.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On Saturday, Shane bought twice as many boxes of plums as boxes of cherries. He also bought 3 boxes of blueberries. How many boxes of cherries did Shane buy if he gave the cashier $100.00 and received $14.50 in change?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of boxes of cherries that he bought. Since he bought twice as many boxes of plums as boxes of cherries, he bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6072f36e4577a20084d5e518bf7e2f2068ab3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> boxes of plums.\n</p><p>If the cashier gave back <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59dcbb784b99cc06b3ed4a6eac5b08f2c84cc825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$14.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> after Shane gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/6/a9659adf2f3dbf4f9619d4fdc9f95f1abe3dfa51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, then the fruits cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/7/7c7e28c57d2ea4d5ddca6ccd3300c8d64d0a8a1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100.00 - \\$14.50 = \\$85.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"209\" height=\"17\" /> in total. \n</p><p>From the table, we can see that each box of cherries costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc3719c11bac960e400f5099762d5e39f6476d92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, each box of plums costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7d7975b71234a1a73891e9cb9743311cf33e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$3.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and each box of blueberries costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548449edef6f356497f86f09cf9560103142d19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. Since he paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20d585322ecf6554d5b350b06280fa1e93b03ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$85.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> in total, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d366223329d076344a91e3e61622558cf5be3794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c + 3 \\times 2c + 4.50 \\times 3 = 85.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"241\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1d64886f3791ca0db1591f52e1944a8b86d5e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2c + 6c + 13.50 = 85.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fdec3a0c91c06763ff5c08137ce8e744b350b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8c = 85.50 - 13.50 = 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1978139f42c109be98f6afbed06c7b56d41cf9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{72}{8} = \\boxed{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005259\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 60/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 893/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2411/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.446      1 2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   14.446      1 -total\n 37.36%    5.397      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36935:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005259 and revision id 285741. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}